{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Subalgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Subalgebra.Lattice","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Conj","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Rat","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":43,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.exists_markovTrace_param_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.exists_markovTrace_param_ne","kind":"theorem","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L405-L413","doc":"**The two Markov parameters are genuinely independent**: the axioms admit a\nmodel with `z ≠ z'`, so the inverse-stabilisation axiom `markov_inv` is not a\nrestatement of `markov`.  Witness: the unit `2` over `ℚ`, whose inverse is\n`2⁻¹ ≠ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L395-L403","doc":"The witness satisfies a quadratic relation, with `h = u - u⁻¹`.  This is what\nkeeps the hypothesis of `MarkovTrace.gen_inv_eq_of_quadratic` and\n`MarkovTrace.markovParam_inv_eq_sub` from being empty: it is inhabited, and with\n`h ≠ 0` whenever `u ≠ u⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace_g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace_g","kind":"theorem","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L392-L393","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace_zinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace_zinv","kind":"theorem","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L389-L390","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace_z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace_z","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L387-L387","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace","kind":"def","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L368-L385","doc":"The one-dimensional tower over `R` with generator a fixed unit `u`, trace the\nidentity, `z = u` and `z' = u⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_ginv_of_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_ginv_of_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L341-L355","doc":"**The inverse-stabilisation axiom itself is derived**, not merely its\nparameter.  Given the quadratic relation, `tr (a * ginv n) = (z - h) * tr a` for\nevery `a ∈ H n`.\n\nThe proof uses only `gen_inv_eq_of_quadratic` (hence `ginv_mul`), linearity of\n`tr`, and `markov` — the field `markov_inv` is **not** used, which is what makes\nthis the honest form of the claim that the fourth Markov axiom is a consequence\nof the other three rather than an independent assumption.  `markovParam_inv_eq_sub`\nis the corresponding statement about the parameter, and does go through\n`markov_inv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.markovParam_inv_eq_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.markovParam_inv_eq_sub","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L327-L339","doc":"**The negative Markov parameter is determined by the positive one** as soon\nas the generator satisfies a quadratic relation: `z' = z - h`.\n\nFor the Iwahori–Hecke relation `σ² = (q - q⁻¹) σ + 1` this reads\n`z' = z - (q - q⁻¹)`, i.e. the fourth Markov axiom is a consequence of the\nother three rather than an independent assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.gen_inv_eq_of_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.gen_inv_eq_of_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L314-L325","doc":"If the generator satisfies a quadratic relation `g n * g n = h • g n + 1`\n— the Hecke relation, with `h = q - q⁻¹` — then its inverse is forced:\n`ginv n = g n - h • 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_genInvWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_genInvWord","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L307-L310","doc":"The trace of a bare ascending word of `k` inverse generators is `z' ^ k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_genWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_genWord","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L300-L305","doc":"The trace of a bare ascending word of `k` positive generators is `z ^ k` —\nthe algebraic counterpart of the `k`-fold stabilised unknot (no link is defined\nhere; see the module docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_genInvWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_genInvWord","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L295-L298","doc":"Iterated stabilisation by the inverse generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_genWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_genWord","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L290-L293","doc":"Iterated stabilisation by the positive generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_stabWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_stabWord","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L267-L288","doc":"**Iterated Markov stabilisation.**  For any family `s` that stabilises with\nconstant factor `c`, appending the `k` successive stabilising elements\n`s n, s (n+1), …, s (n+k-1)` to an element of `H n` multiplies the trace by\n`c ^ k`.\n\nStated for a general `(s, c)` so that it applies verbatim to the positive\ngenerators with `c = z` and to the inverse generators with `c = z'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.stabWord_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.stabWord_mem","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L255-L265","doc":"An ascending word of length `k` starting at level `n` lies in `H (n + k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_gen_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_gen_inv","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L248-L251","doc":"The negative Markov parameter is the trace of an inverse generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_gen","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L242-L246","doc":"The positive Markov parameter is the trace of a generator.  This is where\nthe normalisation axiom `tr 1 = 1` is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_conj_gen_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_conj_gen_inv","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L235-L238","doc":"Conjugating by the inverse of a tower generator leaves the trace\nunchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_conj_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_conj_gen","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L231-L233","doc":"Conjugating by a tower generator leaves the trace unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_eq_of_isConj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_eq_of_isConj","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L223-L229","doc":"**The trace is a class function.**  Conjugate elements have equal trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_conj_units","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_conj_units","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L219-L221","doc":"Conjugation invariance in its unit form: `tr (u * x * u⁻¹) = tr x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_conj","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L210-L217","doc":"**Conjugation invariance.**  Only a *one-sided* inverse is needed: if\n`v * u = 1` then `tr (u * x * v) = tr x`, for every `x`.  Neither `u` nor `v`\nneed be a unit, and `x` is arbitrary.\n\nThis is the algebraic content of Markov move I (whose topological reading is\nthat conjugating a braid does not change its closure — not proved here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.stabWord_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.stabWord_add","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L194-L202","doc":"Concatenation: the ascending word of length `j + k` starting at `n` splits\nas the length-`j` word at `n` times the length-`k` word at `n + j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.stabWord_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.stabWord_succ","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L191-L192","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.stabWord_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.stabWord_zero","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L189-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.stabWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.stabWord","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L183-L187","doc":"The ascending word `s n * s (n+1) * ⋯ * s (n+k-1)`, associated to the\nleft. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.markov_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.markov_inv","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L174-L174","doc":"**(T3')** Markov stabilisation by the inverse generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.markov","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L172-L172","doc":"**(T3)** Markov stabilisation, at the top of the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.zinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.zinv","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L170-L170","doc":"The Markov parameter for a negative crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.z","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L168-L168","doc":"The Markov parameter for a positive crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_one","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L166-L166","doc":"**(T2)** Normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L164-L164","doc":"**(T1)** The trace property. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.tr","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L162-L162","doc":"The trace, as an `R`-linear functional on the whole algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.mul_ginv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.mul_ginv","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L160-L160","doc":"`ginv n` is a right inverse of `g n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.ginv_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.ginv_mul","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L158-L158","doc":"`ginv n` is a left inverse of `g n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.ginv_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.ginv_mem","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L156-L156","doc":"The inverse generator also lives one level up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.ginv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.ginv","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L154-L154","doc":"A two-sided inverse for `g n` (the negative crossing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.g_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.g_mem","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L152-L152","doc":"`g n` lives one level up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.g","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L150-L150","doc":"The generator adjoined at step `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.H_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.H_mono","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L148-L148","doc":"The tower is increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.H","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L146-L146","doc":"The tower of subalgebras `H 0 ⊆ H 1 ⊆ ⋯`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace.MarkovTrace","kind":"structure","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OcneanuTrace.lean#L132-L174","doc":"A **Markov (Ocneanu) trace** on a tower of subalgebras of `A`.\n\n`H n` is the `n`-th algebra of the tower and `g n` is the generator adjoined at\nstep `n`, so `g n ∈ H (n + 1)` but in general `g n ∉ H n`.  `ginv n` is a\ntwo-sided inverse for it, present so that the negative-crossing stabilisation\naxiom can be stated.\n\nEvery field is used by a theorem below, and no field encodes any of the\nconclusions: conjugation invariance, the values `tr (g n)` and `tr (ginv n)`,\niterated stabilisation, and the relation between the two Markov parameters are\nall derived. ","signatureChunk":0}]}